{
  "$comment": "Console route → MCP tool / CLI command map, checked by scripts/check-surface-parity.mjs (pnpm check:surface-parity). Keys are METHOD + Hono path. Each entry names \"mcp\" tools, \"cli\" commands (without 'mushi'), or an \"allow\" reason code from \"reasons\"; \"note\" is free text. \"dynamicCalls\" maps an admin file to the first-argument text of a console call whose path the check cannot resolve, with the reason; a listed call that no longer exists fails as stale.",
  "reasons": {
    "jwt-only": "The route accepts only a signed-in console session (jwtAuth). MCP tools and the CLI authenticate with an API key, so they cannot call it. Widening its auth is a deliberate decision; after that, map a tool or command here.",
    "public": "Unauthenticated or signature-checked endpoint (public pages, invitation preview, webhook receivers, push key). The console links to it or calls it anonymously; it is not an operator action.",
    "console-ui": "Feeds console chrome only (sidebar badges, page stat strips). The data behind it is reachable through the mapped list or detail route.",
    "voice-inbox": "Voice intake has its own clients (iOS Shortcut, Slack, Telegram, the installed console PWA) that call it with a voice:write key; the console page is one of those clients.",
    "credentials": "Enters, replaces or revokes a stored secret or OAuth grant. It stays in the console, where the secret is typed once and never echoed.",
    "editor-equivalent": "The editor reaches the same capability through a different route, named in \"note\".",
    "ci-ingest": "Written by the host app's CI or SDK with an ingest key (apiKeyAuth), not by an operator. The console only shows the URL so CI can be pointed at it; the data it stores is read back through the mapped admin route.",
    "parity-debt": "Accepts an API key but has no MCP tool or CLI command yet. Listed so the debt is visible and can only shrink: add the surface, then replace this entry."
  },
